# Frontend environment variables — self-hosted stack
# (SELFHOST_MIGRATION_PLAN.md Phase 6 / docs/architecture/selfhost-migration.md)
#
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in real values. Never commit .env.local.
#
# ── Supabase is gone ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL, NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY, and
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL have been removed. Post-migration the frontend has no
# database credential and no absolute backend URL of its own: auth and data
# both go through the backend API over a same-origin *relative* path
# (Caddy routes /api/* and /hub/* to the backend in production — see the
# Caddyfile at the repo root and ADR-1 in
# docs/architecture/selfhost-migration.md). There is nothing to configure
# here for a normal `docker compose up` run.
#
# ── Local (non-Docker) dev only ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Running `npm run dev` directly against a backend that isn't behind Caddy
# needs next.config.ts to know where to proxy /api/* and /hub/* in dev
# (docs/architecture/selfhost-migration.md ADR-1). That rewrites() config is
# part of Phase 5 (frontend auth integration), not yet implemented as of
# this file — nothing to set here until then.
# BACKEND_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5000
